#{\footnote what_is}${\footnote What BASILISK SYNTH Is}+{\footnote main:010}K{\footnote BASILISK SYNTH;Sound Recorder;Windows XP;emulator;machine;about}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b What BASILISK SYNTH Is\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 BASILISK SYNTH is a plugin instrument for a {\ul DAW}{\v term_daw}. It is a VST3 for Windows and macOS, and also an Audio Unit and a CLAP on macOS.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Each copy of the plugin runs its own Windows XP in an emulator. In that Windows XP, sixteen copies of Sound Recorder (sndrec32.exe) are open. The plugin calls each copy a {\ul recorder}{\v term_recorder}.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 When you play a note, the plugin chooses a recorder. That Sound Recorder plays its sound through the sound card of Windows XP, at the pitch of your note. The plugin sends that sound to your DAW. The plugin does not make a sound of its own.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The sound is a {\ul DNA}{\v term_dna}: a line of Sound Recorder commands. The plugin keeps the DNA in your project, so the project opens with the same sound.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b When you open the editor\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The editor shows the screen of Windows XP. The sixteen Sound Recorders lose their menu bars, title bars and unused buttons. Then they move into one column, a tape machine of sixteen {\uldb strips}{\v strips}. Task Manager and the Date and Time clock move in beside them. This takes about five seconds. The instrument can play after about one second.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b The first time\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The first time you load the plugin, it downloads the Windows XP machine (788 MB). It checks the file and unpacks it (930 MB). The editor shows the progress. After that, the machine starts in about one second.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 Windows:\tab {\f1 %LOCALAPPDATA%\\BASILISK SYNTH}\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 macOS:\tab {\f1 ~/Library/Application Support/BASILISK SYNTH}\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 To remove the machine, delete that folder.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b See Also\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb Playing the Instrument}{\v playing}\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb The DNA}{\v dna}\par
