#{\footnote playing}${\footnote Playing the Instrument}+{\footnote main:020}K{\footnote playing;notes;MIDI;velocity;sustain pedal;pitch bend;parameters;latency;automation}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b Playing the Instrument\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Put BASILISK SYNTH on an instrument track in your DAW and play MIDI notes. You do not have to open the editor.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b What the instrument uses\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab MIDI notes and their velocity.\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab The sustain pedal (CC64).\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab Pitch bend. The bend applies when a note starts.\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab All Notes Off.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b DAW parameters\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Gain, Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release, Velocity, Bend Range and Transpose. You can automate all of them. Each one changes the {\ul DNA}{\v term_dna}.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Timing\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Each note goes through a whole emulated PC. The plugin tells the DAW a fixed {\ul latency}{\v term_latency} of 100 ms. The DAW moves the sound back by that amount on playback. When you play live, you hear the delay.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Each instrument has sixteen recorders. When all of them play, a new note takes the oldest one. See {\ul voice stealing}{\v term_steal}.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Sleep\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 When no note plays for four seconds and the editor is closed, the machine pauses. The next note or the DAW transport wakes it.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Offline renders\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Windows XP plays in real time, also during an offline render. A render sounds the same as a live bounce.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b To play one strip\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 1\tab Open the editor.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 2\tab Click the Play button of a strip. That recorder plays its sound at its own pitch.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 3\tab Click Stop to stop it.\par
\page
#{\footnote strips}${\footnote The Strips}+{\footnote main:030}K{\footnote strips;recorders;Play button;Stop button;wave display;position;length;slider;colors}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b The Strips\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Each strip is one real Sound Recorder, without its menu bar and title bar. There are sixteen strips, numbered 1 to 16.\par
\pard\sa60\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Number\tab The number of the recorder. Its color shows the {\ul layer}{\v term_layer} that the recorder plays.\par
\pard\sa60\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Play\tab Plays the sound of this recorder. During a note, Play stays down.\par
\pard\sa60\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Stop\tab Stops this recorder.\par
\pard\sa60\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Position\tab The time of the play position, in seconds.\par
\pard\sa60\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Wave\tab The green wave display of Sound Recorder. It follows the sound.\par
\pard\sa60\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Length\tab The length of the sound, in seconds.\par
\pard\sa60\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Slider\tab The position slider. It moves while the recorder plays.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 A note can play more than one recorder. Harmony, unison and layers all add recorders to one note. See {\uldb Voices and Layers}{\v voices}.\par
\page
#{\footnote presets}${\footnote Presets}+{\footnote main:040}K{\footnote presets;factory presets;programs;saving sounds}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b Presets\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 BASILISK SYNTH has 12 factory presets. They are in the preset list of your DAW. Each preset is a {\ul DNA}{\v term_dna}.\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20\b Name\tab DNA\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Chord Organ\tab {\f1 chord#10/ding>>E#6;A2D300S70R250}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Tada Brass\tab {\f1 tada@20[]#16;A5S100R300}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Ding Bells\tab {\f1 ding#8H0,12/xpding#8T12;R600}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Startup Pad\tab {\f1 startup<#16U2~8;A400D800S80R1200}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Reverse Chimes\tab {\f1 chimesR#12U2~6/ding>E#4;A30R500}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Logoff Strings\tab {\f1 logoff@40[#16U3~12;A250S90R900}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Error Pluck\tab {\f1 errorE#16;A0D250S0R150}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Recycle Perc\tab {\f1 recycle>>#8F/xprecycle#8T-12;R80}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Notify Choir\tab {\f1 notify<-E#16H0,7;A300S85R1000}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Critical Bass\tab {\f1 critstop<<#16T-12;A5D400S60R200}\par
\pard\sa35\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Balloon Keys\tab {\f1 balloonMding#16H0,12;R300}\par
\pard\sa60\li2275\ri175\fi-2160\tx2275\plain\f0\fs20 Shutdown Drone\tab {\f1 shutdown<R#16U3~15;A900S100R2000}\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Your own presets\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Save a preset with the preset menu of your DAW. The preset keeps the DNA, so it gives the same sound in each project. A preset from BASILISK 16, the Windows 3.11 edition, also plays here.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b To copy a sound as text\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 1\tab Open the editor.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 2\tab Select the text in the DNA box and press CTRL+C.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 3\tab To use a DNA, paste it into the DNA box and press ENTER.\par
