#{\footnote dna}${\footnote The DNA}+{\footnote main:050}K{\footnote DNA;recipe;Apply;Mutate;Undo;sound, changing}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b The DNA\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The whole sound of the instrument is one line of text, the DNA. Windows XP builds the sound from it with the real menu commands of Sound Recorder, in order from left to right. Because the order changes the result, there are very many different sounds.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Example:\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\plain\f1\fs20 chord#10/ding>>E#6;A2D300S70R250\par
\pard\sa35\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 chord#10}\tab Layer 1: chord.wav on 10 recorders.\par
\pard\sa35\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 /}\tab Starts the next {\ul layer}{\v term_layer}.\par
\pard\sa35\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 ding>>E#6}\tab Layer 2: ding.wav, Increase Speed two times, Add Echo, on 6 recorders.\par
\pard\sa60\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 ;A2D300S70R250}\tab Globals: attack 2 ms, decay 300 ms, sustain 70%, release 250 ms. See {\ul envelope}{\v term_env}.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b To change the DNA\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 1\tab Open the editor.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 2\tab Type in the DNA box, then click Apply or press ENTER.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \tab Or choose a command from the Edit, Effects, Voices or Layers menu. The command goes into the DNA of the selected layer.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 3\tab Windows XP builds the new sound. The DAW gets the new DNA.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\b Mutate} makes one random change: a new step, a new source sound, a harmony, or a mixed-in sound. {\b Undo} goes back to the DNA before the last change.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Rules\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab A DNA has no spaces and is at most 1024 characters.\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab Up to 8 layers, and up to 64 steps in each layer.\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab A step that makes a sound longer than 30 seconds is skipped.\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab Unknown characters are skipped. A number out of range is set to the nearest limit.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab An unknown sound name makes that layer silent.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b See Also\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb DNA Reference}{\v dna_ref}\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb Effects and Edits}{\v effects}\par
