#{\footnote minimize}${\footnote Minimizing the Synth to Use Windows}+{\footnote main:090}K{\footnote minimize;restore;desktop;taskbar;Start menu;Windows XP, using;help, opening;F1}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b Minimizing the Synth to Use Windows\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The synth window covers the whole screen of Windows XP. You can minimize it and use Windows XP as usual: open My Computer, Notepad, Paint or this Help. The instrument keeps playing while it is minimized.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b To minimize the synth\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab On the File menu, choose Minimize.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The taskbar comes back, with a BASILISK SYNTH button on it. The desktop shows the BASILISK SYNTH Help icon.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b To restore the synth\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab Click the BASILISK SYNTH button on the taskbar.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The synth fills the screen again and the taskbar goes away.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b To open this Help\par
\pard\sa35\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab In the synth, press F1, or choose Contents from the Help menu.\par
\pard\sa60\li395\ri175\fi-275\tx395\plain\f0\fs20 \'b7\tab On the desktop, double-click {\b BASILISK SYNTH Help}.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\b Note:} Windows XP in the synth has no network and no sound of its own: its system sounds are off, so they do not play into your music. When you remove the plugin from your project, this Windows XP stops. Changes to its files are not kept.\par
\page
